-- connections.malloy
-- Shared DuckDB connection / path conventions for the MTGJSON models.
--
-- Malloy's duckdb connector reads parquet files directly via
-- duckdb.table('<path>'). Each source file here uses
-- duckdb.table('../data/<file>.parquet'), i.e. the repo-root data/ folder.
--
-- A relative path is NOT resolved against the .malloy file. DuckDB resolves
-- it against the connection's working directory:
--
--   * malloy-cli: the shell's current directory. Run it from inside this
--     folder:  cd Malloy-source-files && malloy-cli run queries.malloy
--   * Publisher: the package directory under publisher_data/. Start it with
--     `--watch-env mtgjson` so that directory is a symlink back to this
--     folder and '../data' lands on the repo-root data/. Without the flag
--     Publisher serves a copy, '../data' points inside publisher_data/, and
--     every source fails with "IO Error: No files found that match the
--     pattern".
--
-- There is no standalone "connection" object to declare here — this file
-- exists as documentation of the convention.
